# Supabase access (this repo)

- **Never** commit or print `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` or service role keys.
- **Always** load Supabase CLI credentials from **`.env.local`** (fallback `.env`) via `scripts/load-env-file.mjs` or `scripts/supabase-cli.mjs`.
- **Do not** rely on `npx supabase login` session alone if `.env.local` has `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` — prefer the wrapper so deploys work in CI/agent shells.
- **Default project ref**: `aqdptcuwpneuyzjavjak` (`supabase/config.toml`). Pass `--project-ref` explicitly when targeting another project.

## Commands

```bash
# Deploy product-intelligence (preferred)
node scripts/deploy-product-intelligence.mjs

# Any Supabase CLI command
node scripts/supabase-cli.mjs functions deploy product-intelligence --use-api
node scripts/supabase-cli.mjs secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=... --use-api
node scripts/supabase-cli.mjs db push
```

## MCP

If Supabase MCP returns Unauthorized, use the CLI wrapper above; MCP may be linked to a different project than this app.
